From ea35136324fc5cb8635af9c397d3e3d71e064c2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:41:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix mobile layout bugs and lengthen splash screens
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by rendering every public page at phone widths (360-390px) with
Playwright against a local static copy, since the live host is not
reachable from this sandbox's network policy:

- Global fix: author CSS was overriding the `hidden` attribute on several
  elements (author display rules beat the UA [hidden]{display:none} rule
  regardless of specificity), most visibly on login.html where the role
  picker and the login form rendered simultaneously instead of the
  intended two-step flow. Added `[hidden]{display:none!important}`
  alongside the existing `.hidden` utility class, which already used the
  same !important pattern for the same reason.
- index.html: a stale `@media(max-width:600px) .business-art{font-size:
  clamp(50px,15vw,70px)}` rule, left over from when that element was one
  giant decorative emoji, was overriding the redesigned info-card version's
  font-size:inherit and blowing card headings up to ~58px, wrapping
  "Organisation accounts" one word per line. Removed the dead rule.
- forgot-password.html: `.auth-card a{color:var(--burgundy)}` had higher
  specificity than `.btn-primary{color:white}`, rendering the "Contact
  support" button's text in burgundy on a burgundy background (invisible).
  Added a scoped override.
- signup.html: the terms checkbox always said "Instructor Terms & Privacy
  Policy" and linked to instructor-policy.html even for student signups;
  now synced to the selected role in syncRole(). Also shortened the
  password placeholder, which was being clipped mid-word on narrow screens.
- verify-certificate.html: gave the h1 a responsive clamp() (it had no
  explicit font-size rule, inheriting an oversized default) and added a
  global `input{text-overflow:ellipsis}` so the certificate-ID placeholder
  clips cleanly instead of hard-cutting mid-character.
- Web splash (splash.js) and native splash (NativeActivity.kt) both only
  guaranteed 400ms/until-session-ready with ~2.5s/4s caps — too short and
  non-deterministic. Both now enforce a 3.2s floor and 5s ceiling.
